Slide 2: The Bottleneck in 3D Construction

Bullet 1: 3D concrete printing promises fast, sustainable housing.

Bullet 2: The Problem: Pre-construction feasibility takes weeks of manual calculation.

Bullet 3: Environmental variables (weather, topology) easily disrupt concrete curing if miscalculated.

Bullet 4: High risk of material waste and regulatory non-compliance.

Slide 3: The EcoStruct AI Solution

Concept: A digital twin feasibility agent.

Function: Users input a site address and building size. The AI autonomously pulls topological, weather, and legal data to generate a complete feasibility report.

Output: Predicts required concrete volume, structural viability, and financial costs in minutes instead of weeks.

Slide 4: System Architecture

Front-End: Python/Gradio interactive dashboard.

The Brain: LangChain + LLM orchestration layer.

The Tools:

Predictive ML: Regression models for cost and material estimation.

RAG Framework: Vector databases for querying municipal building codes.

APIs: GIS mapping and NOAA weather integration.

Slide 5: Testing & Validation

API Testing: Automated queries to ensure reliable external data fetching and error handling.

Back-Testing: Running the predictive ML model against historical data from completed 3D prints to ensure < 5% margin of error.

Hallucination Mitigation: Stress-testing the RAG system to ensure strict adherence to local zoning laws without fabricating data.

Slide 6: Conclusion & Impact

Impact 1: Drastically cuts pre-construction overhead costs.

Impact 2: Eliminates material waste by predicting optimal concrete mixtures.

Impact 3: Accelerates the deployment of sustainable housing solutions.

